<article class="env-proposition" id="0C2W">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0C2W">Proposition <span data-tag="0C2W">55.8.6</span>.</a> Let $C$ be a smooth projective curve over $K$ with $H^0(C, \mathcal{O}_ C) = K$. A minimal model exists. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Choose a closed immersion $C \to \mathbf{P}^ n_ K$. Let $X$ be the scheme theoretic image of $C \to \mathbf{P}^ n_ R$. Then $X \to \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(R)$ is a projective model of $C$ by Lemma <a href="/tag/0C2S" data-tag="0C2S">55.8.1</a>. By Lemma <a href="/tag/0C2U" data-tag="0C2U">55.8.3</a> there exists a resolution of singularities $X' \to X$ and $X'$ is a model for $C$. Then $X' \to \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(R)$ is proper as a composition of proper morphisms. Then we may apply Lemma <a href="/tag/0CD9" data-tag="0CD9">55.8.5</a> to obtain a minimal model. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>